              This keyword specifies what action the admin wishes a user space
              application to take when there is a failure  to  send  an  audit
              event to the kernel. The possible values are: _I_G_N_O_R_E
               -  meaning  do  nothing, _L_O_G - write to syslog the inability to
              send an audit event, and _T_E_R_M_I_N_A_T_E - the user space  application
              should exit.


